    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1065">

                <pb facs="1216" n="1104" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 (China) Thrift Corp./60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-21T18:00:00+08:00">November 21, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—3:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Peiping’s November 18, 4 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d1065-f1"/> Suma<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d1065-f2"/> has informed me today that the Japanese Consul
                    General in Harbin will take measures to prevent the publication in Japanese
                    papers of the attacks connected with the Thriftcor Bank brought to his attention
                    by the American Ambassador.</p>
                <p>By mail to Shanghai, for the Ambassador. Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1065-f1" n="12" xml:id="d1065-f1-content">
